<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I636d4a77ea69d69b5ab18a958e58ee6fcb2476bc" commit="bd017e65461f3df54a23b5c99aca7a308cdc7075" commit_message="Add U2F implementation  Add the common code to support FIDO U2F (Universal second factor authentication) protocol implementation: the APDU parsing and standard commands execution, plus a few non-standard flags and hooks.  The u2f.h header is the unmodified copy from the U2F v1.1 Specifications archive.  Mostly copied over from the cr52 code-base.  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BRANCH=cr50 BUG=b:35545754 TEST=with follow-up CLs, run U2FTest on Eve. CQ-DEPEND=CL:*390230  Change-Id: I636d4a77ea69d69b5ab18a958e58ee6fcb2476bc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/518136 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="518136" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="14" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/36/518136/14" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic2591f369763fb4ba67926e2b4a0c2cd35330a18" commit="5170810676d2e2fb1d06c22376e9b4928763026c" commit_message="cr50: add U2F support  Implement U2F (universal second factor authentication) feature over TPM vendor commands. The raw U2F APDU as defined by the FIDO Alliance 'U2F Raw Message Formats' specification can be sent using the VENDOR_CC_U2F_APDU command. So the vendor command is taking a ISO7816-4:2005 APDU format frame as input as defined by the spec and returns another APDU using ISO7816-4 status code.  The APDU is processed by the common U2F code using u2f_apdu_rcv(), this hardware specific code provides: - the user physical presence detection (done by the power button press)   returned by the pop_check_presence() callback. - the connection to the cryptographic hardware to generate/derive the   keys used by the U2F and individual attestation functions.  This feature/vendor command has 3 modes: - disabled - U2F (only the commands/flags defined by the U2F specification) - G2F (the U2F commands plus some extensions for individual attestation)  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BRANCH=cr50 BUG=b:35545754 TEST=pass U2FTest and HIDTest.  Change-Id: Ic2591f369763fb4ba67926e2b4a0c2cd35330a18 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/518139 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="518139" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/39/518139/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Idc307506dc7a51533b4cde89b90f0d0906b3cdc3" commit="bcf6728f7670ecf0157c1e1635fd064448ed1888" commit_message="driver/timer: Add support for Timer driver  So far only TPM over SPI driver driver was using timer functionality from local scope. Moving required timer functionality into driver code make its easy for other user to access timer function in future.  Change-Id: Idc307506dc7a51533b4cde89b90f0d0906b3cdc3 Signed-off-by: Subrata Banik &lt;subrata.banik@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/555110 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="555110" owner_email="subrata.banik@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/10/555110/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3303c02b3901556b828ba1f5e3899ed742109cfa" commit="5cb7f4becedfdd837a5afecc2c437010766e2144" commit_message="drivers/tpm/spi.c: Using timer function from driver code  Modify internal timer call to make use of timer driver code APIs.  Change-Id: I3303c02b3901556b828ba1f5e3899ed742109cfa Signed-off-by: Subrata Banik &lt;subrata.banik@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/555111 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="555111" owner_email="subrata.banik@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/11/555111/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I05b1fe7ee39fcc52f212ffdba56ef21ffa616e16" commit="338ba38008a7ebf7066741d8762a56fab90850af" commit_message="zoombini: add builder configuration  BUG=b:62462260 TEST=cbuildbot -g '552958' --remote zoombini-release  Change-Id: I05b1fe7ee39fcc52f212ffdba56ef21ffa616e16 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/552958 Commit-Ready: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="552958" owner_email="yueherngl@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/58/552958/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic06794c23af42ffd834cd56fd3454430c8b2a5eb" commit="daf12b1931be5f8945ae98967d2a3c0af7c465e8" commit_message="Remove unnecessary board name from dtsi files  Originally, the design was to have: &lt;board&gt;-private-model.dtsi &lt;board&gt;-model.dtsi  However, the board name isn't set correctly, so the target files end up with: -private-model.dtsi -model.dtsi  This was unnecessary complexity since there will only be one file per image and that file will contain all of the model details, so to fix the issue, we're just going to remove the board prepend.  The consumer of this is a compiler in an ebuild that generates the config.dtb, which already pattern matches on *.dtsi, so that code will remain unaffected.  BUG=b:62997753 TEST=emerge-reef-uni chromeos-base/chromeos-config-bsp  Change-Id: Ic06794c23af42ffd834cd56fd3454430c8b2a5eb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/550875 Commit-Ready: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Tested-by: C Shapiro &lt;shapiroc@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jason Clinton &lt;jclinton@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="550875" owner_email="shapiroc@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/75/550875/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I09352f6551d11b02dc8c81528900e1df793036fb" commit="a7ced6af1865f1a8fbc0fb28f97e3506ba08dbe4" commit_message="Add crosh command to set authpolicy debug level  So far, authpolicyd debug logs were hardcoded to be enabled on dev/canary channels and disabled on beta/stable. This CL removes the hardcoding and adds a crosh command to set authpolicyd's flags default level. This way, debug logs can be easily enabled on any build. Moreover, they are disabled by default on every build, which is preferable from a privacy POV.  BUG=chromium:732339 TEST=Emerge authpolicy and crosh, restart authpolicyd, set level with      authpolicy_debug &lt;level&gt; in crosh, observe /var/lib/authpolicyd.  Change-Id: I09352f6551d11b02dc8c81528900e1df793036fb Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/538715 Commit-Ready: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lutz Justen &lt;ljusten@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Thiemo Nagel &lt;tnagel@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="538715" owner_email="ljusten@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/15/538715/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie28212494ad109bd8caa929a9271fc4c55c5c977" commit="46526bcee567800c81c052b2dc7b459ca7446973" commit_message="Add tegra_bo_import to query tile format.  When a buffer is imported, knowledge of tiling is needed for later calls to map.  Add this functionality for tegra gpus.  The Tegra display engine only knows about 3 compression schemes, of which we only use two (NV_MEM_KIND_C32_2CRA and NV_MEM_KIND_PITCH), these are correlated to DRM_TEGRA_GEM_TILING_MODE_BLOCK and DRM_TEGRA_GEM_TILING_MODE_PITCH respectively in the tegra drm driver.  BUG=chromium:653283, b:38152101 TEST=graphicsSanity on nyan_big  Change-Id: Ie28212494ad109bd8caa929a9271fc4c55c5c977 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/553517 Commit-Ready: Joe Kniss &lt;djmk@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Joe Kniss &lt;djmk@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="553517" owner_email="djmk@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/minigbm" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/minigbm" ref="refs/changes/17/553517/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="9696.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>